    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c674745185524f93a06496d57d1b4171dd34e3b644564ce91a8fe30b1d13ac33",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For weight six with even functional-equation sign, the unit-circle root count reduces to two inequalities among Lambda(f,3), Lambda(f,4), and Lambda(f,5). The paper proves those obligations unconditionally by checking compatible inequalities on every real, critical-line, and off-line zero orbit in the Hadamard product and multiplying the resulting local certificates. Separately, assuming RH for the completed modular L-function, symmetry and nonnegativity of even central Taylor coefficients give a conceptual proof of the boundary inequality (4.2). The conditional Taylor account explains one sign invariant but is not the theorem's unconditional evidence.",
