    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cd029760677f17d28c685dfffd89f264abedbaa3e3ca0c8f74b075c5b6e60e84",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper partitions the proof into two sufficient analytic regions and a reported finite computational remainder. A Pólya-Szegő coefficient criterion covers moderate weights at sufficiently large level, while the exponential-model error budget covers larger weights and complementary level ranges. For the remaining newforms, the authors report high-precision critical-L evaluation, first testing the sufficient coefficient inequalities and, when those fail, directly checking the required trigonometric sign changes rather than treating criterion failure as theorem failure.",
